Vendor credential patterns
--------------------------

The vendor-prefix rules in `pkg/pii/patterns_secret.go` are derived from the
rule catalogue of betterleaks (https://github.com/betterleaks/betterleaks),
itself a fork of gitleaks, which is licensed under the MIT License. That is the
`vendorPrefixes` table and one rule outside it, `clickhouseRe`; the rest of the
catalogue's first tier is this project's own.

What is reused is the set of documented vendor token prefixes and the lengths
each vendor issues -- facts about other companies' credential formats, gathered
there and verifiable against each vendor's own documentation. The expressions
were rewritten for this engine rather than copied: RE2 rather than a boundary
assertion, no case folding over a literal prefix, and, in the table, no trailing
group that consumes a character.

`clickhouseRe` is the exception to that last point, and the reason the scope
above is written by origin rather than by table. Its prefix is four hex
characters, which occur inside any long hash, so the length is the whole of the
evidence and both ends of the span have to be bounded. RE2 has no lookaround, so
each boundary is consumed and the match points at a capture group instead -- and
a rule needing a capture group cannot sit in `vendorPrefixes`, which has no
field for one. Same origin, different table.

The rules that identify a credential by the *name* beside it, rather than by the
value, are not reused at all -- this engine already reads that shape.

